note SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
note Allen's look, the show: what the firmware loop draws each frame and where. Native resolution
note (Lg[0] x Lg[1], the GOP mode), the frame Nfrm (look-paint.om) composed in allen_ui.c's order:
note night base, lights, the merger flash, Allen's being, his words and the bar; in repository mode
note the repository screen (repository-screen.om, drawn through surface.om at native scale) on top.
note Only rectangles that changed are composed; their rows are blitted from two persistent BGRA
note halves (Efa rows 0..hh-1, Efb rows hh..h-1; each at most 16 MiB, the compiler's array limit).
note Sh: 0 ms at start, 1 last t, 2 rows per half (hh), 3 full redraw pending, 4 frames drawn,
note 5 repository screen dirty, 6 last full-screen compose ms, 7 fade strip, 8 the request is
note with the Spark (thinking), 9 the fade's last full pass is done, 10 the ripple radius last
note drawn, 11 now (ms), 12 the ripple was on screen last frame, 13 pixels composed this frame,
note 14 rectangles composed this frame, 15 this frame redrew the whole screen (look-stat.om).
global Sh long 16
global Efa uchar 16777216
global Efb uchar 16777216
global Shrow uchar 2176
global Shd long 1280
global Shdn ulong 1
global Shr long 4
global Shl long 10
global Shb long 20
global Shbn ulong 1
const SHRECTS ulong 320
const SHBORN ulong 12300
const SHFADE ulong 6800
const SHMERGE ulong 12000
const SHGONE ulong 15600
const SHCOARSE ulong 0
fn shfits w ulong h ulong to bool
if or lt w 640 lt h 400
ret false
end
if or gt w 3840 gt h 2176
ret false
end
hh = div add h 1 2
ret le mul mul hh w 4 len Efa
end
fn shclipr x long y long w long h long to bool
note Shr becomes (x,y,w,h) held inside the screen; false when nothing is left.
x1 = add x w
y1 = add y h
if lt x 0
x = 0
end
if lt y 0
y = 0
end
if gt x1 get Lg 0
x1 = get Lg 0
end
if gt y1 get Lg 1
y1 = get Lg 1
end
put Shr 0 x
put Shr 1 y
put Shr 2 sub x1 x
put Shr 3 sub y1 y
if or le sub x1 x 0 le sub y1 y 0
ret false
end
ret true
end
fn shmark x long y long w long h long to void
note Remember a rectangle to compose this frame. Past the list's room, the whole screen is marked.
if not shclipr x y w h
ret
end
n = get Shdn 0
if ge n SHRECTS
put Sh 3 1
ret
end
at = mul n 4
put Shd at get Shr 0
put Shd add at 1 get Shr 1
put Shd add at 2 get Shr 2
put Shd add at 3 get Shr 3
put Shdn 0 add n 1
end
fn shmarkall to void
put Sh 3 1
end
fn shrowa i ulong at ulong n ulong to void
note n pixels from Nfrm[i..] as BGRA into Efa[at..] (rows of the upper half).
for k ulong n
c = get Nfrm add i k
put Efa at uchar and c 255
put Efa add at 1 uchar and shr c 8 255
put Efa add at 2 uchar and shr c 16 255
put Efa add at 3 0
at = add at 4
end
end
fn shrowb i ulong at ulong n ulong to void
note The same into Efb (rows of the lower half).
for k ulong n
c = get Nfrm add i k
put Efb at uchar and c 255
put Efb add at 1 uchar and shr c 8 255
put Efb add at 2 uchar and shr c 16 255
put Efb add at 3 0
at = add at 4
end
end
fn shrow y ulong x0 ulong n ulong to void
note One row's pixels x0..x0+n-1 from Nfrm into the BGRA half that holds row y.
w = ulong get Lg 0
hh = ulong get Sh 2
i = add mul y w x0
if lt y hh
shrowa i mul i 4 n
else
shrowb i mul add mul sub y hh w x0 4 n
end
put Shrow y 1
end
fn shconvert x long y long w long h long to void
note Nfrm -> BGRA for the rectangle, and its rows are remembered for the blit.
for r ulong ulong h
shrow add ulong y r ulong x ulong w
end
end
fn shblit y0 ulong rows ulong to bool
note Rows y0..y0+rows-1 (whole width) to the screen from the half that holds them; a run that
note crosses the halves is sent as two.
w = ulong get Lg 0
hh = ulong get Sh 2
if and lt y0 hh gt add y0 rows hh
if not shblit y0 sub hh y0
ret false
end
ret shblit hh sub add y0 rows hh
end
arg = or or w shl rows 32 shl y0 48
n = mul mul w rows 4
put Stw 10 add get Stw 10 n
st = ulong 0
if lt y0 hh
st = efi 3 arg Efa mul mul y0 w 4 n
else
st = efi 3 arg Efb mul mul sub y0 hh w 4 n
end
ret eq st 0
end
fn shflush to bool
note Blit every run of rows marked by shrow, then clear the marks.
h = ulong get Lg 1
y = ulong 0
ok = true
while lt y h bound 2176
if eq get Shrow y 0
y = add y 1
else
n = ulong 0
while and lt add y n h ne get Shrow add y n 0 bound 2176
put Shrow add y n 0
n = add n 1
end
if not shblit y n
ok = false
end
y = add y n
end
end
ret ok
end
fn shrepo to void
note The repository screen, through surface.om at native scale, over the composed sky.
if ne get Dmo 0 1
ret
end
ok = ghrender
end
fn shcompose x long y long w long h long to void
note allen_ui.c compose: night base, lights, flash, the being, words and bar.
pkclip x y w h
ntbase x y w h
ntlights x y w h 0 0
hmflash x y w h
mddraw x y w h
hmtext x y w h
end
fn shfull to void
note The whole screen, then the repository screen if it is up, then BGRA.
w = get Lg 0
h = get Lg 1
shcompose 0 0 w h
shrepo
shconvert 0 0 w h
put Sh 13 mul w h
put Sh 14 1
put Sh 15 1
put Shdn 0 0
put Sh 3 0
end
fn shrects to void
note Every marked rectangle: compose and convert. Rectangles may overlap; drawing twice is harmless
note because every layer is a pure function of position and time.
n = get Shdn 0
px = long 0
for i ulong n
at = mul i 4
x = get Shd at
y = get Shd add at 1
w = get Shd add at 2
h = get Shd add at 3
shcompose x y w h
shconvert x y w h
px = add px mul w h
end
put Sh 13 px
put Sh 14 long n
put Sh 15 0
put Shdn 0 0
end
fn shtwinkles to void
note The twinkling stars' boxes (ck_night_star_box) as in allen_ui.c: every star, every frame.
n = ntcount
for i ulong n
ntstarbox i
shmark get Pa 0 get Pa 1 get Pa 2 get Pa 3
end
end
fn shstrip to void
note The eyes adjust over 6.8 s in slow patches: the screen is composed a sixth at a time, so a
note frame stays cheap and every part of the sky is refreshed about twice a second.
h = get Lg 1
k = rem get Sh 7 6
y0 = div mul h k 6
y1 = div mul h add k 1 6
shmark 0 y0 get Lg 0 sub y1 y0
put Sh 7 add get Sh 7 1
end
fn shchord r long dy long to long
note Half the width of a circle of radius r at dy from its centre (0 outside).
if ge dy r
ret 0
end
ret long pkisqrt ulong sub mul r r mul dy dy
end
fn shringband hi long lo long ya long yb long to void
note The ring between radii lo and hi within rows ya..yb-1: one rectangle, or two when the band
note misses the ring's hollow middle. Distances are from (cx, cy).
cy = get Lg 4
cx = get Lg 3
near = long 0
if gt ya cy
near = sub ya cy
end
if lt yb cy
near = sub cy yb
end
far = pkmax pkabs sub ya cy pkabs sub yb cy
xo = shchord hi near
xi = shchord lo far
if eq xo 0
ret
end
if eq xi 0
shmark sub cx xo ya mul xo 2 sub yb ya
else
shmark sub cx xo ya sub xo xi sub yb ya
shmark add cx xi ya sub xo xi sub yb ya
end
end
fn shring to void
note The ripple bends the sky only within reach of its crest (night.c in_ripple); since the last
note frame the crest moved out, so the band from the old inner edge to the new outer edge changes.
r = get Ntrip 0
w = get Ntrip 1
if eq w 0
ret
end
reach = add div mul w 22 10 9
hi = add r reach
lo = sub get Sh 10 reach
if or lt lo 0 eq get Sh 10 0
lo = 0
end
put Sh 10 r
cy = get Lg 4
ya = sub cy hi
if lt ya 0
ya = 0
end
yend = add cy hi
if gt yend get Lg 1
yend = get Lg 1
end
while lt ya yend bound 64
yb = add ya 64
if gt yb yend
yb = yend
end
shringband hi lo ya yb
ya = yb
end
end
fn shbadd x long y long w long h long to void
note A box onto the list Shb (at most 5: two holes now, two before, one spare).
n = get Shbn 0
if ge n 5
ret
end
at = mul n 4
put Shb at x
put Shb add at 1 y
put Shb add at 2 w
put Shb add at 3 h
put Shbn 0 add n 1
end
fn shbmeet a ulong b ulong to bool
note Do boxes a and b of Shb overlap (share at least one pixel column and row).
a = mul a 4
b = mul b 4
if ge get Shb a add get Shb b get Shb add b 2
ret false
end
if ge get Shb b add get Shb a get Shb add a 2
ret false
end
if ge get Shb add a 1 add get Shb add b 1 get Shb add b 3
ret false
end
if ge get Shb add b 1 add get Shb add a 1 get Shb add a 3
ret false
end
ret true
end
fn shbjoin a ulong b ulong to void
note Box a becomes the union of a and b; the last box moves into b's place.
n = get Shbn 0
a = mul a 4
b = mul b 4
x1 = add get Shb a get Shb add a 2
y1 = add get Shb b get Shb add b 2
x1 = pkmax x1 y1
y1 = add get Shb add a 1 get Shb add a 3
x0 = add get Shb add b 1 get Shb add b 3
y1 = pkmax y1 x0
x0 = pkmin get Shb a get Shb b
put Shb a x0
x0 = pkmin get Shb add a 1 get Shb add b 1
put Shb add a 1 x0
put Shb add a 2 sub x1 get Shb a
put Shb add a 3 sub y1 get Shb add a 1
n = sub n 1
put Shbn 0 n
n = mul n 4
for i ulong 4
put Shb add b i get Shb add n i
end
end
fn shbmerge to void
note Join overlapping boxes until none overlap: every layer is a pure function of position and
note time, so one union costs less than two boxes composed twice where they meet.
for pass ulong 8
joined = false
n = get Shbn 0
for a ulong n
for b ulong n
if and lt a b not joined
if shbmeet a b
shbjoin a b
joined = true
end
end
end
end
if not joined
ret
end
end
end
fn shlens to void
note The holes' lens boxes now (Shl remembers them for the next frame) and the boxes of the
note frame before, merged where they meet, then marked.
put Shbn 0 0
n = ulong get Shl 8
for i ulong n
at = mul i 4
shbadd get Shl at get Shl add at 1 get Shl add at 2 get Shl add at 3
end
put Shl 8 0
for i ulong ntholes
if ntholebox i
shbadd get Pa 0 get Pa 1 get Pa 2 get Pa 3
k = ulong get Shl 8
at = mul k 4
for j ulong 4
put Shl add at j get Pa j
end
put Shl 8 add long k 1
end
end
shbmerge
n = get Shbn 0
for i ulong n
at = mul i 4
shmark get Shb at get Shb add at 1 get Shb add at 2 get Shb add at 3
end
end
fn shdecide t ulong to void
note Which parts of the screen change at t (ms since the sky started). Sh[9]: the fade's last
note full pass is done; Sh[12]: the ripple was on screen last frame; Shl: the lens rect last frame.
if lt t add SHFADE 400
shstrip
else
if eq get Sh 9 0
put Sh 9 1
shmarkall
end
end
if ne get Ntrip 1 0
shring
put Sh 12 1
put Ntcoarse 0 SHCOARSE
else
put Ntcoarse 0 0
if ne get Sh 12 0
put Sh 12 0
shmarkall
end
end
note The holes' lens regions now and where they were, Allen, his words and bar, the twinkles.
shlens
mddirty
shmark get Mdbox 0 get Mdbox 1 get Mdbox 2 get Mdbox 3
shmark get Hmdirty 0 get Hmdirty 1 get Hmdirty 2 get Hmdirty 3
shtwinkles
end
fn shstep now ulong to bool
note Move the show on to now and draw what changed. False when the screen refused a blit.
if eq get Sh 0 0
put Sh 0 long now
end
put Sh 11 long now
t = sub now ulong get Sh 0
ntat t
hmstep long t
mdat long t
if eq get Dmo 0 1
note Repository mode: a still picture, redrawn only when the screen says it changed.
if or ne get Sh 5 0 ne get Sh 3 0
shfull
put Sh 5 0
ret shflush
end
ret true
end
shdecide t
if ne get Sh 3 0
shfull
else
shrects
end
put Sh 1 long t
put Sh 4 add get Sh 4 1
t1 = efms
ok = shflush
shstat now t1 efms t
ret ok
end
fn shstat t0 ulong t1 ulong t2 ulong t ulong to void
note The frame's clocks and what it composed, for the stopwatch (look-stat.om).
rf = ulong add mul get Sh 14 2 get Sh 15
stframe t0 t1 t2 t ulong get Sh 13 rf
end
fn shsubmit to void
note Enter in the bar: a recognised repository request opens the repository screen; anything else
note goes to the Spark through the courier (look-chat.om) and Allen thinks until the answer comes.
n = get Hminn 0
if or eq n 0 gt n 159
ret
end
for i ulong n
put In i get Hmin i
put Dprm i get Hmin i
end
put Inlen 0 n
put Dprmn 0 n
if stasked
hmkey 13
ret
end
if inmatch
hmkey 13
ininstall ulong get Sh 11
ret
end
if ghask
put Dmo 0 1
put Sh 5 1
hmkey 13
ret
end
if eq get Es 6 0
ret
end
if chask ulong get Sh 11
put Sh 8 1
hmthink 1
end
hmkey 13
end
fn shkey key ulong to bool
note Keys: the repository screen takes them while it is up (Escape closes it); otherwise the bar.
if eq get Dmo 0 1
if eq key 27
put Dmo 0 0
ghinit
shmarkall
ret true
end
ghkey key
put Sh 5 1
ret true
end
if or eq key 10 eq key 13
shsubmit
ret true
end
hmkey key
ret true
end
fn shanswer to void
note The courier's visible text becomes what Allen says.
if ne get Chevent 0 1
if or eq get Chevent 0 5 eq get Chevent 0 6
if eq get Chevent 0 6
hmthink 0
put Sh 8 0
end
put Chevent 0 0
end
ret
end
n = get Chsayn 0
if gt n len Hmsay
n = len Hmsay
end
for i ulong n
put Hmsay i get Chsay i
end
put Hmsayn 0 n
hmsaid
hmthink 0
put Sh 8 0
put Chevent 0 0
end
fn shinit now ulong to bool
note Sizes from the screen (Es), then every module of the look.
w = get Es 0
h = get Es 1
if not shfits w h
ret false
end
put Lg 0 long w
put Lg 1 long h
kw = div mul w 256 1920
kh = div mul h 256 1080
if lt kh kw
kw = kh
end
put Lg 2 long kw
put Lg 3 long div w 2
put Lg 4 long div mul h 40 100
put Sh 2 long div add h 1 2
for i ulong 2176
put Shrow i 0
end
put Shdn 0 0
put Shl 8 0
pkinit
ntinit
mdinit long SHBORN
hminit
put Sh 0 long now
put Sh 3 1
ret true
end
